From 060ec6970b052fa10bed1db73bb586a1fed4b70f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shanks <shanks@book>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:38:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/37] feat(transportd): implement hookpoint=v3 passthrough
 (Go owns the request)

v3 replaces the inputs of the request-construction step only. The auth
injection closure (session.rs 237-238 in the switch commit), the retry loop,
the timeout and the SSE relay stay byte-identical.

- codex-api: stream_raw_bytes_with / execute_raw_bytes_with take
  Option<RequestBody> and call no configure closure; stream_raw_passthrough /
  execute_raw_passthrough feed RequestBody::Raw + RequestCompression::None, so
  ctd neither compresses nor writes content-encoding/content-type (the Raw
  branch of prepare_body_for_send only clones headers and body).
- transportd/transport/responses_v3.rs: responses and compact both filter the
  Go header set through V3_HEADER_ALLOWLIST, then check required headers,
  content-encoding <-> body shape, and the header self-consistency audit --
  all before any upstream I/O. Failure is always fail-closed; v3 never falls
  back to v1 (that would poison the A/B comparison).
- chatgpt_provider_bare keeps ctd from injecting its own version when Go did
  not deliver one (HeaderMap::extend replaces same-name keys but keeps
  provider-only ones).
- contract/headers.rs: X-CTD-Outbound-Headers, V3_HEADER_ALLOWLIST,
  V3_REQUIRED_HEADERS, V3_AUDIT_HEADERS, V3_CONTENT_ENCODINGS, and a
  spec-driven carrier parser shared with the v1 channel. Outbound headers are
  parsed only when hookpoint == v3, so a v1 request carrying the channel is
  unaffected.
- v1 path unchanged: same functions, same arguments, only re-indented.

Tests: cargo test -p codex-transportd (174 lib + all integration suites) and
cargo test -p codex-api pass. The two lifecycle/uds tests fail on this machine
only because umask is 0000 and tempfile therefore creates world-writable dirs,
which verify_socket_parent_dir rejects; they pass under umask 077 and the guard
is untouched by this change.
